# Networking Fundamentals: Components, Types, Connections, Infrastructure & ISP

## 1. Network Components

Network components are devices and media that allow communication between systems.

### End Devices
- Computer
- Laptop
- Smartphone
- Server
- IoT devices

### Intermediary Devices
- Router – Connects different networks
- Switch – Connects devices within a LAN
- Hub – Broadcasts data to all devices
- Firewall – Provides security
- Access Point – Provides wireless connectivity
- Modem – Connects network to ISP

### Transmission Media
- Twisted Pair Cable (Ethernet)
- Coaxial Cable
- Fiber Optic Cable
- Wireless (Wi-Fi, Bluetooth)

---

## 2. Types of Networks

### Based on Coverage Area
- PAN (Personal Area Network)
- LAN (Local Area Network)
- MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)
- WAN (Wide Area Network)

### Based on Architecture
- Client–Server Network
- Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Network

---

## 3. Network Connections

### Wired Connections
- Ethernet cable
- Fiber optic cable

Advantages:
- High speed
- Stable
- Secure

### Wireless Connections
- Wi-Fi
- Bluetooth
- Cellular networks

Advantages:
- Flexible
- Easy installation
Disadvantages:
- Less secure than wired
- Possible interference

---

## 4. Network Infrastructure

Network infrastructure is the complete setup that supports network communication.

Includes:
- Networking hardware (routers, switches, servers)
- Software (network operating systems)
- Protocols (TCP/IP, HTTP, FTP)
- Security systems (firewall, IDS/IPS)
- Data centers
- Cloud services

Purpose:
- Reliable communication
- Security
- Scalability
- Performance

---

## 5. ISP Connectivity

ISP (Internet Service Provider) provides internet access to users.

### Working Flow
User Device → Router → Modem → ISP → Internet

### Types of ISP Connections
- DSL
- Fiber
- Cable
- Satellite
- Mobile data

---

## Key Points
- Network components enable communication.
- Infrastructure supports and manages the network.
- Different network types exist based on size and design.
- ISP connects local networks to the global internet.
